Found downstream in rex-rancher k25 (fixed there in 0b97665). lib/Rex/GPU.pm POD (~lines 90-125, HEAD 26f0adf) says several die paths (unsupported Debian release, V100+B200 mix, vGPU guest in install_driver, Debian 11/openSUSE) happen "before the host is changed" / "before anything on the host is changed". Not strictly true:
- gpu_detect -> Detect::_ensure_lspci installs pciutils when lspci is missing, before any die in plan.
- Dies in resolve_plan (source missing only visible after an index refresh, e.g. Ubuntu with no fitting driver package / nvidia-driver-580-server without candidate) come after prepare_host/prepare_source: unattended-upgrades + apt-daily stopped, contrib/non-free enabled (Debian), cuda-keyring + repo + apt-get update; RHEL EPEL/CRB, CUDA repo, dnf module enable/versionlock; SUSE rpm -e of existing nvidia*/libnvidia* + zypper addrepo.
Accurate wording already exists: Setup/Ubuntu.pm "dies before any driver package is installed", plan POD "known without a refreshed package index". Align GPU.pm POD with that (before any driver package is installed; at most pciutils, or prepared package sources for index-dependent dies). Doc only; verify against current source first.

